// The handoff's core repro (module-namespaces): `use std.http` is a valid namespace group, but
// `http.get(...)` names no member of it — `get` lives on the `http.client` submodule. A group is
// fully enumerable, so both backends reject this at check time (E0005). `check` and `run` now AGREE.
// expect: error E0005 at 7:5
// expect: exit 1
use std.http
r = http.get("https://svc.test/echo")
echo "unreachable"
